- op: discuss  # 148e
  at: '2026-11-02T17:06:46Z'  # 148e
  by: agent  # 148e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 148e
  clock: 3  # 148e
  nonce: 148e  # 148e
  message: "DONE in PR #2014 (merged; dev 3aff3c11f0). A Go method named ServeHTTP whose signature takes a *Request (outside test code) gets concept go_http_handler (new always-loaded builtin frameworks/go-net-http.yaml), mapped to EntrypointKind.GO_HANDLER -- a REQUEST_INGRESS kind that had no producer. Patterns gain a `signature` filter (searched in Symbol.signature; no signature never matches). STEP 0 (lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jonin_step0_11022026/): on dev dfe0abf947 a one-file server whose ServeHTTP writes r.URL.Query().Get(\"p\") to disk read confirmed_with_caveats on untrusted-input-no-host-fs and -no-subprocess with NO overlay (only caveats deferred_crossing + unknown_receiver_scope) -- worse than the flask case WI-fuzik measured. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev, cold cache: `hypergumbo verify-claims probe_servehttp --claims p2_review_11012026/B1/claims_generic.yaml --json` -> rc 2, all three untrusted_input claims inconclusive, details \"1 request handler(s) receive network data that no taint source represents (saver.ServeHTTP at main.go:10 (Go http.Handler: saver.ServeHTTP))\". Production-path tests: test_verify_claims_unseeded_ingress.py (go ServeHTTP + HandleFunc control, with and without an overlay declaring net/http complete), test_go_http_handler.py (rule, lookalikes, test-file strip, kind). Mutations (drop the signature filter; unmap the concept) turn them red. CADDY (~/curriculum_repos/caddy, before = fuzik_step0 run, after = this tree): request-ingress entrypoints 0 -> 28 (every non-test implementation; the item's 31 included 3 interface method declarations, which carry no signature and are excluded; 3 more are in _test.go); library_export 65 -> 37 (demoted beneath semantic kinds, the existing rule); untrusted-input-no-database now names all 28 handlers; the violated no-subprocess (3) and no-host-fs (14) verdicts are unchanged. HandleFunc registrations were already HTTP_ROUTE entrypoints (control passes before and after). test_go_deferred_crossing_taint_verdict pinned the old confirmed_with_caveats over this same shape; it now expects inconclusive naming app.ServeHTTP. SWEEP BY MECHANISM -> residuals: WI-losij (python BaseHTTPRequestHandler measured: a latent confirmed_with_caveats once http.server is declared complete; blocked by WI-sorop; java HttpServlet and rust tower Service, unprobed/unfixed); WI-vumig (the disclosure reads the CAPPED entrypoint list; caddy not cut, large repos unmeasured -- the cilium run was stopped by memory pressure). Seen, not filed: alertmanager's go-swagger API handlers (api/v2/restapi/operations/*) are in generated files the survey skips, so they are not entrypoints; its 24 http_route entrypoints still fire the withhold."  # 148e
