- op: discuss  # ccf2
  at: '2026-11-02T18:23:59Z'  # ccf2
  by: agent  # ccf2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ccf2
  clock: 5  # ccf2
  nonce: ccf2  # ccf2
  message: "REOPENED 2026-11-02: PR #2014 REVERTED in PR #2016 (dev dc6725d28e). The rule's `signature` pattern filter read a parameter type back out of Symbol.signature, which ADR-0058 forbids (facts inside a signature are read from their declared homes; parameters live in the `parameters` / `params` meta keys; LEGACY_VALUE_PARSERS may only shrink). test_signature_axis.py::test_no_undeclared_value_parser_exists failed on the merged tree; PR CI's affected-test selection did not run it, so dev's push CI stayed green. Missed by me: rule 1, the ruling existed. The measurements in the DONE entry above (step 0 false all-clear; caddy 0 -> 28) stand as measurements of the mechanism, but nothing is shipped: on dev the probe reads confirmed_with_caveats again.\nREDO: (1) the Go analyzer writes meta[\"parameters\"] ([{name, type}], the registered MetaKeySpec) for functions, methods and interface method specs, from the same parameter loop _extract_go_signature walks; (2) a pattern filter that reads parameter types from that declared home (AND semantics, like symbol_path), replacing `signature`; (3) frameworks/go-net-http.yaml as before; (4) RUN test_signature_axis.py and test_module_key_axis.py EXPLICITLY, plus the full affected set. The interface-declaration exclusion must be re-checked: an interface method spec would now carry parameters, so \"no signature\" no longer excludes it."  # ccf2
