- op: discuss  # 1b08
  at: '2026-11-02T21:24:47Z'  # 1b08
  by: agent  # 1b08
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1b08
  clock: 7  # 1b08
  nonce: 1b08  # 1b08
  message: "DONE (redo) in PR #2018 (merged; dev ba432fd845). Replaces #2014 (reverted in #2016 for parsing Symbol.signature, ADR-0058). Nothing reads the signature now. (1) go.py writes meta[\"parameters\"] (overload_arity.parameter_entry: name, type, variadic) for functions, methods and interface method specs from the parameter list, receiver excluded; a spec has no body and carries the abstract modifier (the marking cpp/kotlin give an abstract member). Go stable ids unchanged (hashed from the signature). (2) framework_patterns: parameter_type declared beside symbol_name is an AND and decisive; no existing rule declared both, parameter_type alone unchanged. (3) frameworks/go-net-http.yaml: method named ServeHTTP, parameter_type ^\\*(\\w+\\.)?Request$, modifiers_exclude ^abstract$, never in test code -> go_http_handler -> EntrypointKind.GO_HANDLER (0.90). BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev, cold cache: hypergumbo verify-claims jonin_step0_11022026/probe_servehttp --claims p2_review_11012026/B1/claims_generic.yaml --format json -> rc 2; untrusted-input-no-subprocess / -no-host-fs / -no-database all inconclusive, naming saver.ServeHTTP at main.go:10 (Go http.Handler: saver.ServeHTTP). Before (dev): confirmed_with_caveats with no overlay. CADDY (this tree vs the reverted fix): the identical 28 go_handler entrypoints (28 of 28 same symbols); of 37 ServeHTTP symbols, the 3 interface specs are excluded by abstract (positive, not an absent signature), 3 are in test files, 3 are external stubs; untrusted-input-no-database inconclusive naming 28 handlers; violated verdicts unchanged (lab ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jonin_redo_11022026/). test_signature_axis and test_module_key_axis run explicitly and listed in the PR manifest. Mutations (AND off, abstract exclusion off, method parameters off, abstract marking off) each redden only their own tests. Residuals unchanged: WI-losij, WI-vumig."  # 1b08
